From e5cb967190fee212f8da910d37dfe1f604769eb8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chiro <chiro2001@163.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 02:42:10 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 194/254] perf(cpu): execute SVE256 int8 layout ops natively
 (q10-sve256-int8-layout)

Admit int8 reshape/view/contiguous/transpose/slice/split/concat on the
SVE256 native descriptor plane: new ptx_layout_i8/ptx_split_i8/ptx_concat_i8
kernels plus the layout v4 / indexing v5 wires, so the W8A8 weight
transpose that blocked Q5 lowers and executes natively instead of
fail-closed. The native contract predicate is shared by artifact metadata
and runtime dispatch (declaration==execution); unsupported dtypes stay
fail-closed. f32/bf16 layout lanes now reproduce the host reference's
CPython-float round trip (including signaling-NaN quieting) bit-for-bit.
TypedByteView gains int8 so int8 payloads stay raw bytes across the wire.
Bump lowering 8->9, artifact payload 1->2, runner protocol v6->v7, layout
wire 3->4, indexing wire 4->5; pre-Q10 artifacts fail closed.
